              %em On Categories of Monoids, Comonoids and bimonoids
              (doi:
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2989/QM.2008.31.2.2.474"}> 10.2989/QM.2008.31.2.2.474
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://user.informatik.uni-bremen.de/porst/dvis/CoBiMon_Porst.pdf"} pdf
          %p Free monoid constructions are discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eduardo+Dubuc"}> Eduardo Dubuc
                ,
                %em Free monoids
                Algebra J. 29, 208–228 (1974)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Kelly"}> Max Kelly
                ,
                %em A unified treatment of transfinite constructions for free algebras, free monoids,colimits, associated sheaves, and so on
                Bull. Austral. Math. Soc. 22(1), 1–83 (1980)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Lack"}> Stephen Lack
                ,
                %em Note on the construction of free monoids
                Appl Categor Struct (2010) 18:17–29
          %p The detailed discussion of pushouts along free monoid morphisms is in the proof of lemma 6.2 of
          %ul#SchwedeShipley
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
